---
title: Japanese Curry-Roux Bricks
description: Japanese curry roux from scratch, with white miso and ten ground spices, chilled into bricks.
tags: [make-ahead]
course: condiment
icons: [cubes-stacked, mortar-pestle, pot-food]
cuisine: Japanese
source:
  name: America's Test Kitchen
  url: https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/15954-japanese-curry-roux-bricks
yield: 2%bricks
time: 55m
---

Stir the @sugar{1 1/2%tsp}, @ground turmeric{1 1/2%tsp}, @ground coriander{1 1/2%tsp}, @ground ginger{1 1/2%tsp}, @ground cardamom{1/2%tsp}, @ground cumin{1/2%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1/2%tsp}, @ground fennel{1/2%tsp}, @ground fenugreek{1/2%tsp}, @garlic powder{1/2%tsp}, @ground brown mustard{1/4%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/4%tsp} together in a #bowl{}.

Melt the @unsalted butter{8%tbsp} in a 10-inch #skillet{} over low heat.

Off the heat, sprinkle the @all-purpose flour{2/3%cup} over the butter and #whisk{} until smooth.

Return the skillet to medium heat and cook, whisking very frequently, until the flour mixture is pale golden brown, ~cook{3-4%minutes}.

Remove from the heat and immediately whisk in the spices. Add the @white miso{1%tbsp} and whisk until very well combined (the mixture will not be totally smooth).

Transfer the mixture to a #loaf pan{} and smooth it into an even layer. Refrigerate until fully set, about ~chill{30%minutes}.

Run a #knife{} around the edge of the pan to release the curry brick. Remove the brick and cut it into 2 equal pieces.

> **Storing** — Bricks can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 1 week or frozen for up to 3 months.
